session_id: taker_flow_exhaustion_mvp_20261011_v1
market: crypto
thesis: >-
  Following a complete 1-hour candle with extreme directional taker quote-volume imbalance
  and an aligned price move under normal-or-higher trading volume, temporary
  aggressive execution demand overshoots fundamental value. A position opposite
  that candle direction held four hours has positive net expectancy after fees.
mechanism: >-
  Liquidity demand from urgent buyers or sellers temporarily displaces quotes;
  replenishing order-book liquidity can reverse some price impact. The signal
  fails when informed flow initiates a persistent trend.
falsifier: >-
  Reject this single frozen, cost-aware rule in its 2026 development sample if
  net portfolio return is non-positive, no valid trades occur in either asset,
  or simulated maximum drawdown exceeds 10 percent. Positive results remain
  exploratory and do not establish live or prop-firm viability. No tuning.
